WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.753
Military service definitely
has humbled me as an individual,

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:09.384
and it also allows you to be
more compassionate with others.

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:12.220
My name is Violeta Ware
and I am a Marine

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:13.888
and an Army veteran.

00:00:13.972 --> 00:00:16.975
When 9/11 came, I knew that
I wanted to serve myself.

00:00:17.225 --> 00:00:19.144
And so when I turned 17,

00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:20.687
I received a waiver
from my parents

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:23.314
to enlist in the ROTC program
at Georgia Tech.

00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:25.191
I also served,
enlisted in the Army,

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.360
and then I answered
the call in the government

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.237
and served there for six
and a half years.

00:00:29.237 --> 00:00:31.239
I am a construction
engineer by trade,

00:00:31.239 --> 00:00:34.451
and I function as a utilities
project manager in facilities.

00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:36.244
The Belonging at Yale program

00:00:36.244 --> 00:00:39.247
allows all of us an opportunity
network with each other.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:42.041
There are large disparities
with veterans who come home

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:43.877
and fight battles
that are silent.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:47.172
The struggles are internal
and we need everyone's support.

00:00:47.255 --> 00:00:49.340
To my fellow veterans
on Veterans Day,

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.426
I encourage you guys
to share your stories

00:00:51.426 --> 00:00:54.220
with each other and fellowship
in all of our service.

